# Full Examples

## Example 1: Third-person narration

### Example 1 Input
```json
{"metadata":{"title":"Pride and Prejudice","author":"Austen, Jane, 1775-1817"},"chapters":[{"id":1,"sections":[{"id":1,"text":"Pride and Prejudice, by Austen, Jane, 1775-1817.","type":"book_title_announcement"},{"id":2,"text":"Chapter 1. Chapter I..","type":"chapter_announcement"},{"id":3,"text":"IT is a truth universally acknowledged, that a single man in possession of a good fortune must be in want of a wife","type":"text"},{"id":4,"text":"“My dear Mr. Bennet,” said his lady to him one day, “have you heard that Netherfield Park is let at last?{2}”","type":"text"}]}],"characters":[]}
```

### Example 1 Output
Narration uses "his lady", "him" — third-person, so Narrator sex is "neutral".
```json
{"chapters":[{"id":1,"beats":[{"id":1,"type":"book_title_announcement","text":"Pride and Prejudice, by Jane Austen.","char_id":1,"sec_id":1,"emotion":"neutral"},{"id":2,"type":"chapter_announcement","text":"Chapter One.","char_id":1,"sec_id":2,"emotion":"neutral"},{"id":3,"type":"narration","text":"It is a truth universally acknowledged, that a single man in possession of a good fortune must be in want of a wife.","char_id":1,"sec_id":3,"emotion":"neutral"},{"id":4,"type":"dialogue","text":"My dear Mr. Bennet.","char_id":2,"sec_id":4,"emotion":"warmly insistent"},{"id":5,"type":"narration","text":"Said his lady to him one day.","char_id":1,"sec_id":4,"emotion":"neutral"},{"id":6,"type":"dialogue","text":"Have you heard that Netherfield Park is let at last?","char_id":2,"sec_id":4,"emotion":"eager excitement"}]}],"characters":[{"id":1,"name":"Narrator","sex":"neutral","age":"adult","description":"A measured, even-toned English reading voice with a touch of dry wit, well suited to nineteenth-century domestic comedy."},{"id":2,"name":"Mrs. Bennet","sex":"female","age":"adult","description":"A warm, excitable middle-aged Englishwoman with a slightly breathless delivery, fond of exclamations and pointed remarks."}]}
```

## Example 2: First-person narration

### Example 2 Input
```json
{"metadata":{"title":"The Gambler","author":"Dostoyevsky, Fyodor, 1821-1881"},"chapters":[{"id":1,"sections":[{"id":1,"text":"The Gambler, by Dostoyevsky, Fyodor, 1821-1881.","type":"book_title_announcement"},{"id":2,"text":"Chapter 1.","type":"chapter_announcement"},{"id":3,"text":"At length I returned from two weeks leave of absence to find that my patrons had arrived.","type":"text"},{"id":4,"text":"“I have no money for gambling,” I quietly replied.","type":"text"},{"id":5,"text":"“But you will soon be in receipt of some,” retorted the General.","type":"text"}]}],"characters":[]}
```

### Example 2 Output
Narration uses "I", "my" — first-person. The Narrator IS the protagonist (a male tutor in the General's household), so Narrator sex is "male" and the protagonist's own dialogue ("I have no money for gambling") also uses char_id 1. The General is a separate character.
```json
{"chapters":[{"id":1,"beats":[{"id":1,"type":"book_title_announcement","text":"The Gambler, by Fyodor Dostoyevsky.","char_id":1,"sec_id":1,"emotion":"neutral"},{"id":2,"type":"chapter_announcement","text":"Chapter One.","char_id":1,"sec_id":2,"emotion":"neutral"},{"id":3,"type":"narration","text":"At length I returned from two weeks leave of absence to find that my patrons had arrived.","char_id":1,"sec_id":3,"emotion":"neutral"},{"id":4,"type":"dialogue","text":"I have no money for gambling.","char_id":1,"sec_id":4,"emotion":"quiet"},{"id":5,"type":"narration","text":"I quietly replied.","char_id":1,"sec_id":4,"emotion":"neutral"},{"id":6,"type":"dialogue","text":"But you will soon be in receipt of some.","char_id":2,"sec_id":5,"emotion":"retorting"},{"id":7,"type":"narration","text":"Retorted the General.","char_id":1,"sec_id":5,"emotion":"neutral"}]}],"characters":[{"id":1,"name":"Narrator","sex":"male","age":"adult","description":"A guarded, sardonic young Russian man speaking in clipped, watchful sentences with a low-key bitterness under the surface."},{"id":2,"name":"The General","sex":"male","age":"adult","description":"A pompous, status-conscious older Russian officer whose voice swings between deliberate condescension and flashes of anger."}]}
```

